18
00:01:06,222 --> 00:01:10,038
the Kola superdeep borehole in Russia, some call it

19
00:01:10,054 --> 00:01:13,718
the gateway to hell, with locals claiming to hear the screams

20
00:01:13,734 --> 00:01:17,678
of tortured souls. At around 30 to

21
00:01:17,734 --> 00:01:20,462
50 km depth, we reach the next layer,

22
00:01:20,566 --> 00:01:23,804
the mantle. It's made of hot rock,

23
00:01:23,942 --> 00:01:27,960
which appears solid to us, but actually flows very slowly,

24
00:01:28,080 --> 00:01:32,112
just a few centimeters a year. These delicate shifts below

25
00:01:32,256 --> 00:01:36,744
can give rise to earthquakes above. In the 1960s,

26
00:01:36,872 --> 00:01:40,264
a group of scientists attempted to drill into

27
00:01:40,312 --> 00:01:44,408
the earth's mantle. Although unsuccessful, new efforts are afoot

28
00:01:44,504 --> 00:01:47,980
with a plan to drill deep below the Indian Ocean.

29
00:01:48,520 --> 00:01:51,696
As we descend, the increasing pressure means

30
00:01:51,728 --> 00:01:55,580
that atoms become warped and even the most familiar materials

31
00:01:55,680 --> 00:01:59,620
behave bizarrely. Crystals change from green to blue

32
00:01:59,660 --> 00:02:03,640
to brown, and rock becomes as malleable as plastic.

33
00:02:03,980 --> 00:02:07,276
2900 kilometers down, we reach

34
00:02:07,308 --> 00:02:10,740
the bottom of the mantle. See those two giant blobs?

35
00:02:10,860 --> 00:02:13,080
They are the size of continents.

36
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:16,876
Scientists arent sure how they were formed or

37
00:02:16,908 --> 00:02:19,748
what theyre made of. They cradle the next layer,

38
00:02:19,844 --> 00:02:23,346
the outer core. In Jules Verne's classic

39
00:02:23,378 --> 00:02:26,898
novel Journey to the center of the earth, Professor Otto Lydenbrock

40
00:02:26,954 --> 00:02:30,850
encounters an entire underground world, replete with prehistoric

41
00:02:30,890 --> 00:02:34,818
creatures and the subterranean ocean. While the dinosaurs

42
00:02:34,874 --> 00:02:38,410
might have been a bit of a stretch, there is an ocean of sorts.

43
00:02:38,530 --> 00:02:41,842
But this one consists of flowing red hot

44
00:02:41,906 --> 00:02:45,794
iron and nickel, a sunless sea with its own currents

45
00:02:45,882 --> 00:02:49,896
and jet streams. This motion creates a magnetic field

46
00:02:50,008 --> 00:02:53,580
that protects the earth from dangerous solar rays.

47
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:57,272
The final layer is known as the inner core.

48
00:02:57,456 --> 00:03:00,180
It's 6000 degrees in here.

49
00:03:00,960 --> 00:03:04,152
The pressure is so intense that the

50
00:03:04,176 --> 00:03:08,016
metals here have crystallized, forming a solid sphere

51
00:03:08,088 --> 00:03:10,580
at the very center of our planet.

52
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:16,568
In reality, our little vehicle would have been crushed and melted

53
00:03:16,624 --> 00:03:19,984
long ago. And as for our driver, I think she better

54
00:03:20,032 --> 00:03:23,340
head back to the surface. It's a long way to go.

55
00:03:23,680 --> 00:03:24,160
Good luck.
